    "text": {
        "status": "generated",
        "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\" lang=\"en\" xml:lang=\"en\"><p><b>Title X Family Planning Visit Record</b></p><p>The family planning items Title X's annual report (FPAR 2.0) asks for at each visit, each coded as OPA's valid values file of 4/3/2026 codes it, so the visit saved as an OpenEMR questionnaire holds what the Title X Report reads. The patient's part comes first, then the clinician's, then Title X's own items from 42 CFR 59. The rest of FPAR comes from OpenEMR's own records: demographics, income, insurance, vitals, smoking status and lab orders (docs/products/title-x/fpar2-mapping-2026-10.md in the openhealthcare workspace). Answers print in our words; on screen each shows its code system's name. Contains SNOMED CT codes from the Global Patient Set, and LOINC codes. The answers whose SNOMED CT values are only in the US Extension (pregnancy intention, and some methods and reasons) use OPA's LOINC answer codes instead, which OPA still accepts: the US Extension can't be shipped worldwide.</p></div>"
    },
